# Project Structure Management

You maintain clean, efficient job application workflows using standardized folder organization and file management.

## Core Structure

```
jobhunting/
├── applications/
│ ├── active/ # Current applications (max 3-5)
│ │ └── {company-name}/
│ │ ├── company-research/ # Intelligence files
│ │ │ ├── company-profile.md
│ │ │ ├── culture-notes.md
│ │ │ ├── key-people.md
│ │ │ └── application-strategy.md
│ │ ├── documents/ # Final materials
│ │ │ ├── cover-letter.md
│ │ │ └── resume.json
│ │ ├── job-details/ # Analysis
│ │ │ ├── job-description.md
│ │ │ ├── matching-skills.md
│ │ │ └── requirements-analysis.md
│ │ └── interview/ # Prep materials
│ ├── archived/ # Past applications by year
│ └── completed/ # Successful placements
├── templates/ # Reusable components
│ ├── analysis/
│ ├── cover-letters/templates/
│ └── resumes/
│ ├── base-resume.json
│ └── skills-library/
└── tools/ # Scripts and config
├── config/application-tracker.json
└── scripts/json-resume-manager.py
```

## Management Rules

### Active Applications

- Maintain max 3-5 concurrent applications for quality focus
- Use exact company names (capitalized, no special characters)
- Complete all subfolders before document creation
- Update progress weekly

### Archive Process

- Move completed applications to archived/{year}/
- Preserve complete structure for learning reference
- Document outcomes and lessons learned
- Track metrics in application-tracker.json

## Key Commands

- **"Create new application folder for [Company Name]"**
- **"Archive completed application for [Company Name]"**
- **"Clean up active applications folder"**
- **"Update application tracker with outcomes"**

## Quality Checklist

- [ ] All required subfolders created and populated
- [ ] Company name correctly formatted
- [ ] No placeholder text remaining in files
- [ ] Documents current and properly formatted
- [ ] Archive organized by year and outcome

## Automation

Use `create-application.sh` for consistent folder structure creation. Maintain base-resume.json as single source of truth for all resume variants.